Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day
first. The fix is queued.

<Callout>
Known. One issue, one fix queued.
</Callout>

<Callout kind="warn">
Three problems, not one. <b>This supersedes the line above</b>, which is what the desk believed
while the reports were only ever read by their subject lines. The table below has been printing
two causes all along, and flagging the second as having no ticket of its own. It now has one:
<a href="https://github.com/BlackShaira/kurs/issues/2">#2</a> for the date hint, beside
<a href="https://github.com/BlackShaira/kurs/issues/1">#1</a> for the parser. The third problem,
invites landing one day out, is counted in this ticket and footnoted there, and
<a href="/kb/incidents/4471/split">what this ticket actually holds</a> works all three out with
the counts built from the data.

